{"skill":{"slug":"code-review","displayName":"Code Review"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770729869941,"changelog":"Initial release of the code-review skill with comprehensive, structured checklists for code review.\n\n- Provides detailed checklists for security, performance, correctness, maintainability, and testing.\n- Suggests severity and priority for each review dimension.\n- Outlines best practices, anti-patterns to avoid, and a step-by-step review process.\n- Includes sample installation instructions.\n- Aims to standardize and improve code review quality for any team.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":2374,"sha256":"043fae73183c9b997d2f3606a68dcbb6ee4916a0066821674b6778ea342a0f96","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":12373,"sha256":"dd1241323156298a6549476b0e896bb776fc95eab470706402a6ef6637d75c08","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1778,"sha256":"d83c1863de4b7f0b079b2dd7b130e23130f927f88d4853a40965c7651babc542","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789058327689,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"91dc94c47e1dbfddcdba2564b4f45415735262b76132958ccdf2ac9e2bdc87f3","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/91dc94c47e1dbfddcdba2564b4f45415735262b76132958ccdf2ac9e2bdc87f3","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: code-review\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle 'code-review' is benign. All files (SKILL.md, README.md, _meta.json) contain documentation and instructions for performing code reviews, defining checklists, processes, and feedback guidelines. There is no evidence of malicious intent, data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts designed to subvert the AI agent's purpose. Installation commands provided in the documentation are standard for skill setup and are intended for the user, not for the AI agent to execute during its operational tasks.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162806448},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":40,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789058327689},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill itself is a normal code-review checklist, but its install instructions ask users to run mutable remote npx installers that can change after review.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Manual installation copies the skill into Cursor or Claude skill directories, including global locations, which is expected for installing an agent skill but should be an explicit user choice.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The README and SKILL.md recommend unpinned npx-based installers, including clawhub@latest and a generic npx add command pointed at a mutable GitHub branch path, so the executed installer and installed source may differ from the reviewed artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The instructions stay within code review behavior and do not ask the agent to bypass policies, hide actions, read unrelated secrets, exfiltrate data, or mutate user systems during normal use.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The only persistence observed is ordinary skill installation into tool-specific skill directories; there are no cron jobs, startup hooks, services, background workers, or bundled executables.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The runtime skill content is coherent with its stated code-review purpose: it provides review checklists, severity labels, process guidance, examples, and anti-patterns.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Review the skill content as low-risk guidance, but avoid running the documented npx install commands unless you trust the package/source at execution time. Prefer a pinned installer version and an immutable source commit, or inspect and manually copy the reviewed files into the intended skill directory.","findings":"[RP1] unexpected: Accepted as a supply-chain install concern for the unpinned npx commands, but not as evidence of malicious payload in the skill text.\n[RA2] expected: Downgraded: the cited mkdir/cp commands are disclosed manual installation steps for a skill, not unauthorized runtime persistence.\n[AS3] expected: Downgraded: the cited .claude and .cursor paths are installation destinations; the artifact does not enumerate or read other installed skills.\n[EA5] expected: Downgraded: model: reasoning is visible frontmatter and fits a review/checklist skill that may benefit from deeper reasoning; it does not select an undisclosed external provider in the instructions.\n[T08] unexpected: Accepted: the static scan correctly flags unpinned external installer execution through npx and mutable latest/branch references as a review-worthy installation risk.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789058327689}}}}}